paid so far. Expected shows the confirmed cost, while the separate forecast also keeps remaining commitments. For a $1,000 job with a $200 deposit, Actuals can be $200 while Expected final remains $1,000. Variance uses Expected, not simply payments to date.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "FAQ & troubleshooting",
-    "title": "Why can I not close a Paid line?",
-    "body": "<p>Check outstanding expected refunds, missing payment receipts and unreviewed legacy opening Actuals. Attach evidence, record/cancel legitimate return expectations and review legacy values. Finalize cost and Close line are different; neither should be used to hide genuine unpaid obligations.</p>"
+    "title": "What should I review after a line is paid?",
+    "body": "<p>Paid lines can still have missing receipts, expected refunds or legacy opening values requiring review. Attach evidence and record or cancel legitimate refund expectations. Previously closed or finalized lines can be reopened from the line; their history is preserved.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "FAQ & troubleshooting",
